{"updateDevice returns ErrDeviceLimitReached for any unknown device, not just limit-exceeded ones \u2014 a new device that has never been inserted will always produce 0 rows affected, conflating 'device not found in DB' with 'device limit reached'": 0.9521214365959167, "Wire-registered ProvideAnonDBStore receives no deviceLimit parameter \u2014 wire cannot inject a bare int64 from *setting.Cfg, so the wire-bound *AnonDBStore will be constructed with deviceLimit = 0, disabling the device limit entirely": 0.7316821217536926, "The AnonDeviceServiceAPI receives a zero-limit store via wire while ProvideAnonymousDeviceService constructs its own inline *AnonDBStore with cfg.AnonymousDeviceLimit, making the two stores inconsistent": 0.5417879223823547, "FakeAnonStore does not implement the full AnonStore interface \u2014 missing DeleteDevice and DeleteDevicesOlderThan methods, causing compilation failures when used as AnonStore": 0.05465928837656975, "Auth client layer directly imports and checks DB-layer sentinel error anonstore.ErrDeviceLimitReached, creating a layering violation where the authentication client depends on the storage layer": 0.5597909092903137, "No test for Authenticate returning error when ErrDeviceLimitReached \u2014 the critical new blocking behavior is completely untested at the Authenticate level": 0.5857555270195007, "FakeService doesn't support configuring a TagDevice error, only ExpectedError for CountDevices": 0.10448138415813446, "ProvideAnonymousDeviceService constructs AnonDBStore directly instead of accepting an AnonStore interface parameter, breaking dependency injection and mock substitution in tests": 0.7517412304878235, "Tests in impl_test.go access anonService.anonStore directly (an unexported field) to call ListDevices, which is a test-layer boundary violation": 0.23395085334777832, "Local cache is populated before CreateOrUpdateDevice succeeds, so a device blocked on first request will be silently allowed through on subsequent requests within the 29-minute cache TTL": 0.7035858631134033, "AnonymousDeviceLimit is exposed in frontend settings to unauthenticated users, unnecessarily disclosing internal capacity configuration": 0.4931275546550751, "Go DTO declares AnonymousDeviceLimit as int64 (always present) while TypeScript type declares it as number | undefined, creating a type mismatch": 0.647141695022583, "Test TestIntegrationBeyondDeviceLimit does not verify that existing devices can still be updated when limit is reached": 0.2566289007663727, "No device ID length/content validation \u2014 arbitrarily long device IDs accepted, potentially causing excessive memory usage in local cache or oversized DB entries": 0.057718053460121155, "TypeScript anonymousDeviceLimit type inconsistent with Go int64 backend \u2014 frontend code checking === undefined to detect 'no limit' will never be true": 0.537421464920044, "anonymousDeviceExpiration constant duplicated across three packages (anonstore/database.go, api/api.go, and impl.go) requiring synchronized updates": 0.5098603963851929}